  "title": "Dr. John's Gumbo",
  "country": "US",
  "released": "1972-04-00",
  "notes": "[l130920] pressing denoted by PR plant code in label matrix and dual, humped pressing ring of 1\" and 2 3/4\" diameter.\nA Specialty pressing with a single pressing ring and \"PR\" plant codes on labels exists - see [r=9632234].\n\nHeavy gatefold cover. With insert that includes a short bio and a breakdown of each track as told to Jerry Wexler.\n\nSome copies of this pressing were used for promo, with an added \"Promotional DJ Copy\" sticker on the front cover with suggested cuts for airplay listed.\n\n\"Thanks to [a132067] of the J. Geils Band for the suggestion to cut Iko Iko.\"\n\nFifth album by New Orleans R&B artist Dr. John, a tribute to the music of his native city. The album is a collection of covers of New Orleans classics, played by a major figure in the city's music.\n\nTitle listed as \"Gumbo\" on both spine and labels.\n\nRunouts are etched.",
  "released_formatted": "Apr 1972",
